      "en": ["At the time of its construction, the Chain Bridge was regarded as an engineering marvel and was one of the largest suspension bridges in the world.", "According to a popular urban legend, the sculptor of the guardian lions threw himself into the Danube when it was pointed out that the lions had no tongues.", "The bridge was completely blown up by retreating German troops at the end of World War II and was rebuilt and reopened exactly 100 years after its original inauguration.", "The bridge is beautifully illuminated at night, transforming the iron chains into a glowing necklace draped across the river."]
