      "en": ["The Göcsej Village Museum in Zalaegerszeg was the very first open-air museum (Skanzen) established in Hungary, opening in 1968.", "The city is home to the highly unique Hungarian Oil and Gas Industry Museum, featuring massive, open-air displays of historic drilling rigs and machinery.", "Zalaegerszeg features one of the most stunning, modern Catholic churches in the country, the Church of the Immaculate Heart of Mary, designed by Imre Makovecz.", "The city has recently become a major European hub for automotive technology, hosting the massive, state-of-the-art ZalaZONE autonomous vehicle test track."]
